NNAAMMEE
       mklost+found  - create a lost+found directory on a mounted Linux second
       extended file system

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       mmkklloosstt++ffoouunndd

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       mmkklloosstt++ffoouunndd is used to create a _l_o_s_t_+_f_o_u_n_d directory  in  the  current
       working  directory  on  a  Linux second extended file system.  There is
       normally a _l_o_s_t_+_f_o_u_n_d directory in the root directory of each file sys‐
       tem.

       mmkklloosstt++ffoouunndd  pre-allocates  disk blocks to the _l_o_s_t_+_f_o_u_n_d directory so
       that when ee22ffsscckk(8) is being run to recover a file system, it does  not
       need  to  allocate blocks in the file system to store a large number of
       unlinked files.  This ensures that ee22ffsscckk will  not  have  to  allocate
       data blocks in the file system during recovery.

